4.1 Constrained optimization problem
\[
\min_{x\in\mathbb{R}^n} f(x), \quad \text{s.t.}\quad
\begin{cases}
G_i(x) = 0, & i\in\mathcal{E} \quad\to\ \text{equality constrained} \\
G_i(x) \geq 0, & i\in\mathcal{I} \quad\to\ \text{inequality constrained}
\end{cases}
\]

6.2 Inequality Constrained Case
\[
\min_{x\in\mathbb{R}^n} f(x), \qquad \text{s.t.}\quad G_i(x)=0,\ i\in\mathcal{E};\quad G_i(x)\geq 0,\ i\in\mathcal{I}.
\]
\[
\Rightarrow \min_{p} \nabla f(x_k)^{\mathsf T}p + \tfrac{1}{2}p^{\mathsf T}\nabla^2\mathcal{L}(x_k,\lambda_k)p, \qquad
\text{s.t.}
\begin{cases}
G_i(x_k) + \nabla G_i(x_k)^{\mathsf T}p = 0, & i\in\mathcal{E} \\
G_i(x_k) + \nabla G_i(x_k)^{\mathsf T}p \geq 0, & i\in\mathcal{I}
\end{cases}
\]
which is solved with an inequality QP.

